It is a beautiful Saturday morning.
I leave my flat.
I go to my bicycle and get on.
Today is my very first shift.
I have decided to help at a neighbourhood café on the weekend.
I have worked a lot on my laptop this week.
Now I want to meet people outside the tech world.
I ride through the quiet streets.
At the second traffic light, I ride to the left.
The sun is shining and the air is warm.
I am excited, but also a little nervous.
I have never worked in a café before.
Today I am learning to make good espresso.
The café is only ten minutes away.
I already see the tables on the pavement.
I park my bicycle.
My new adventure begins.
